> >
> > Anyway, for this, the bit you definitely want to be fiddling with is
> > the parts of mapglyph() where (x == u.ux && y == u.uy) is being
> > tested, and setting the 'color' variable there.
> 
> Before testing for states I wanted to try to see if I could just
> arbirtarily change the heros color thusly:
> 
> 	    if (iflags.use_color && x == u.ux && y == u.uy &&
> 		    iflags.showrace && !Upolyd)
> /*		color = HI_DOMESTIC;*/
> 		color = CLR_CYAN;
> 
> Compiled and ran it and the hero is still white.  Am I missing
> something?

That code only kicks in if you have showrace set; it's to force the
glyph white even if the generic monster for your race is a different
colour. With !showrace, the whiteness of the hero glyph is picked up
directly from the mcolor field of your role monster. You're going to
want to break up that condition whatever you do.

